-- title:
--   Residue sum zero for Γ₀(N)-invariant weight-two functions
-- statement:
--   Fix a positive level $N$ and let $F_N$ denote the field $\mathbb{C}$-generated inside $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ \mathbb{C}$ by the coefficientwise images of the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ \mathbb{Q}$ generated by the $q$-expansions $\mathrm{qExpand}\ \mathbb{Q}\ d\ jq$ for the divisors $d \mid N$, i.e. [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange ℂ (ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldFull N)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103); a place of $F_N$ over $\mathbb{C}$ is a valuation subring containing $\mathbb{C}$, not equal to all of $F_N$, and a principal ideal ring. Let $D$ be a complex place dictionary of level $N$: a map $\tau \mapsto P_\tau$ from the upper half plane to such places together with positive integers $e_\tau$, invariant under the action of $\Gamma_0(N)$, such that $x$ lies in the valuation subring $P_\tau$ exactly when $\|\mathrm{realize}\ N\ x\|$ is bounded near $\tau$ on the punctured neighbourhood filter, and such that for $x \neq 0$ the meromorphic order at $\tau$ of $z \mapsto \mathrm{realize}\ N\ x\ (\mathrm{ofComplex}\ z)$ equals $e_\tau \cdot \mathrm{ord}_{P_\tau}(x)$. Let $\omega : \mathfrak{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ and let $r$ be a finitely supported $\mathbb{C}$-valued function on the places of $F_N$ over $\mathbb{C}$, subject to: $\omega \mid_2 \gamma = \omega$ for all $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(N)$; for each $\sigma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ there is $\delta > 0$ with $\omega \mid_2 \sigma = O(e^{-\delta \operatorname{Im}\tau})$ along `atImInfty`; every place in the support of $r$ is of the form $P_\tau$ for some $\tau \in \mathfrak{H}$; and for every $\tau \in \mathfrak{H}$ there is $g$ analytic at $\tau$ with $\omega(\mathrm{ofComplex}\ z) = e_\tau\, r(P_\tau)/(z - \tau) + g(z)$ for $z$ near $\tau$, $z \neq \tau$. Then $\sum_{P} r(P) = 0$, the sum over the support of $r$.
--
--   This is the residue theorem for the compact Riemann surface $X_0(N)$, transported to the place-theoretic language used for the function field of $X_0(N)$: the residues of a $\Gamma_0(N)$-invariant weight-two function with at worst simple poles and exponential decay at the cusps add up to zero. It is used to show that a divisor of degree zero is realised as the residue divisor of such a function, in [`ModularCurve.ComplexPlaceDictionary.exists_slashInvariant_residue_eq_of_degree_eq_zero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.ComplexPlaceDictionary.exists_slashInvariant_residue_eq_of_degree_eq_zero).
